<Base title="About">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <img src="/headshot.png" alt="James Coppock" width="160" height="160" style="border-radius:50%" />
  <p>I'm James. I've spent my career on one kind of problem: taking a noisy signal and making it trustworthy enough to act on.</p>
  <p>It started with motion: algorithms for sensors inside footballs at Wilson, then heart rate and blood pressure from wrist and ear sensors at Valencell. At Duke I moved inside the body, building deep-learning models that measure how spinal discs deform in MRI, which became my PhD in Biomedical Engineering. After that came clinical data science at Bionic Health. Now I'm a Senior AI/ML Applied Scientist at Infinia ML, the AI arm of Aspirion, where I architect ContractIQ, a system that follows healthcare all the way to the bill.</p>
  <p>Increasingly my work is about more than models: setting technical direction, shaping product strategy, and helping teams build ML that holds up in the real world.</p>
  <p>I live in Durham, NC, in a historic house we've been <a href="/life/restoration">restoring</a>. When I'm not working, I'm <a href="/life/photography">taking photos</a> or at a <a href="/life/hockey">Canes game</a>.</p>
